<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Entities and metric calculators. CLAUDE.md §Solution layout:
    "Domain references nothing." That is not a style preference — the metric
    definitions in docs/03_METRICS.md are the single source of truth for every
    number the product displays, and they are golden-tested (docs/14_TESTING.md
    requires >= 95% coverage here or the PR fails). Keeping this project free of
    infrastructure is what makes those tests fast and unambiguous.

    Do not add a PackageReference here without changing CLAUDE.md first.
  -->

  <!--
    WHO MAY MINT A CONSENT RECORD, and why the list is short.

    GameConsentRecord.Stored is internal. FrameLedger.App and FrameLedger.Agent
    both reference FrameLedger.Application, which references this assembly, and
    docs/12_BUILD.md publishes both roots into one out/app. A public minting
    factory here would therefore be a blessed, SHIPPED API for producing consent
    nobody gave — and tools/package-closure-check.ps1 could not see it, because
    it walks project references and Domain is legitimately in both closures.

    20_OPEN_QUESTIONS §S27 rejected "HookEnabled = true, ConsentedAt = UtcNow"
    synthesised at a call site as "a gate whose verdict is decided before it
    looks". The point of this list is that the same act stays as visible as that
    string was, instead of reading as a call to a sanctioned API.

    FrameLedger.CaptureHost is the unshipped host that owns the file-backed
    store. When P2 adds a SQLite adapter in FrameLedger.Infrastructure, adding it
    here is the deliberate, reviewable act — not a discovery.

    Test assemblies are on the list because they are not published — no publish
    root references them — and the alternative is a suite that can only exercise
    the refusing default. They are still scanned by tools/chokepoint-check.ps1,
    whose managed pass covers tests/ as well as src/.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="FrameLedger.CaptureHost" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="FrameLedger.Domain.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="FrameLedger.Application.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="FrameLedger.CaptureHost.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
